{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.SYTEncodingBridgeTwo","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SYTEncodingBridgeTwo","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.SYTEncodingBridge","lean:module:Mathlib.Order.Interval.Finset.Nat"],"declarations":15,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SYTEncodingBridge.numSYT_eq_numStandardYoungTableaux","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SYTEncodingBridge.numSYT_eq_numStandardYoungTableaux","kind":"theorem","line":202,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SYTEncodingBridgeTwo.lean#L202-L209","doc":"**The bridge**: the two standard-Young-tableau encodings count the same thing. With it, the RSK\nidentity `OVTopAssembly.sum_numSYT_sq_eq_factorial` (stated with `numSYT`) becomes available to the\nhook-length side (`sytDim`/`numSYTenum`/`numStandardYoungTableaux`), which is what\n`RSKBurnsideTarget.RSKBurnsideHolds` and the Plancherel normalisation\n`Σ_λ (f^λ)² = k!` both need. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SYTEncodingBridge.numSYT_le_numStandardYoungTableaux","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SYTEncodingBridge.numSYT_le_numStandardYoungTableaux","kind":"theorem","line":194,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SYTEncodingBridgeTwo.lean#L194-L200","doc":"**The other half of the bridge**. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SYTEncodingBridge.toMathlibSYT_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SYTEncodingBridge.toMathlibSYT_injective","kind":"theorem","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SYTEncodingBridgeTwo.lean#L169-L192","doc":"The reverse embedding is injective (entries agree on cells after removing the shift, and vanish\noff cells). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SYTEncodingBridge.toMathlibSYT","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SYTEncodingBridge.toMathlibSYT","kind":"def","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SYTEncodingBridgeTwo.lean#L147-L167","doc":"**The 0-indexed encoding embeds into the 1-indexed one**: add one on cells. The semistandard\nfields come from the generalized monotonicity lemmas, and the `Set.BijOn` from the pigeonhole. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SYTEncodingBridge.shift_bijOn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SYTEncodingBridge.shift_bijOn","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SYTEncodingBridgeTwo.lean#L125-L143","doc":"The `Set.BijOn` the 1-indexed structure demands, assembled from maps-to, inj-on and the\npigeonhole. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SYTEncodingBridge.shift_surjOn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SYTEncodingBridge.shift_surjOn","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SYTEncodingBridgeTwo.lean#L110-L123","doc":"**The pigeonhole**: an injection of the `n`-cell set into `{1, …, n}` is onto. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SYTEncodingBridge.shift_injOn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SYTEncodingBridge.shift_injOn","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SYTEncodingBridgeTwo.lean#L100-L108","doc":"The shifted map is injective on the cells. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SYTEncodingBridge.shift_mem_Icc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SYTEncodingBridge.shift_mem_Icc","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SYTEncodingBridgeTwo.lean#L92-L98","doc":"The shifted map lands in `{1, …, |μ|}` on cells. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SYTEncodingBridge.shift_of_not_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SYTEncodingBridge.shift_of_not_mem","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SYTEncodingBridgeTwo.lean#L88-L90","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SYTEncodingBridge.shift_of_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SYTEncodingBridge.shift_of_mem","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SYTEncodingBridgeTwo.lean#L84-L86","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SYTEncodingBridge.shift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SYTEncodingBridge.shift","kind":"def","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SYTEncodingBridgeTwo.lean#L80-L82","doc":"The 1-indexed shift of a 0-indexed tableau: `+1` on cells, `0` off them. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SYTEncodingBridge.entry_lt_col'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SYTEncodingBridge.entry_lt_col'","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SYTEncodingBridgeTwo.lean#L72-L76","doc":"Column monotonicity in the `i1 < i2` form the semistandard structure demands. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SYTEncodingBridge.entry_lt_row'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SYTEncodingBridge.entry_lt_row'","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SYTEncodingBridgeTwo.lean#L66-L70","doc":"Row monotonicity in the `j1 < j2` form the semistandard structure demands. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SYTEncodingBridge.entry_lt_col","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SYTEncodingBridge.entry_lt_col","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SYTEncodingBridgeTwo.lean#L50-L64","doc":"Columns increase strictly over an arbitrary gap. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SYTEncodingBridge.entry_lt_row","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SYTEncodingBridge.entry_lt_row","kind":"theorem","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SYTEncodingBridgeTwo.lean#L33-L48","doc":"Rows increase strictly over an arbitrary gap (induction on the gap; the intermediate cells lie\nin `μ` by the lower-set property). ","signatureChunk":0}]}